theory.intro:
The equation of a line is $y=mx+c$. Read $c$ where the line crosses the $y$-axis, then find $m$ as $\frac{\text{rise}}{\text{run}}$ between two points you can read off the grid.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[gray!45,very thin] (-3,-3) grid (3,3);
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-4.2,0) -- (4.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (0,-3.9) -- (0,3.9) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,{Stealth}-{Stealth}] (-3.9,-1.6) -- (3.9,3.6);
\draw[dashed] (0,1) -- (3,1) node[midway,below,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {run};
\draw[dashed] (3,1) -- (3,3) node[midway,right,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] {rise};
\fill (0,1) circle (2pt);
\fill (3,3) circle (2pt);
\node[above left,fill=white,inner sep=1pt] at (-0.15,1.05) {$c$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
